**P1 — Derive native-script products from the owning recipe stage.** Both actual Mantle recipes contain **740 produced-input references apiece** to nonexistent `full-source-rust-provider/*` actions: `.program`, `.scripts`, `.roots`, and `.zero` for each of 185 native controllers. For example, stage1 step `helper-metadata-link.native.scripts` consumes `full-source-rust-provider/helper-metadata-link.native.program/text`, although its producer is the local `mantle-stage1/helper-metadata-link.native.program/text`; the Rust recipe declares no corresponding action. The local producer has no local consumer or root. `validate_source_recipe` requires every step to be reachable, so stage1 cannot complete preparation before any source action executes. The cause is `src/source_built_rust_programs_llvm.rs:477–506`: `text` and `assemble` return references through a constructor hardcoded to the Rust stage, even when `append_native_source_script` receives a Mantle `SourceRecipe`. Make those returned references use `recipe.stage_id` and regenerate both recipes; do not add cross-stage aliases.

